Exports the `stringify` function directly. The package instead defines it on `globalThis` on
import, so that its CommonJS and ES module entry points share one instance. We bundle a single copy
of the package, so there is nothing to share, and:
- Importing `unutils/json` must not change globals.
- The `sideEffects` field of our `package.json` lets bundlers drop the bare `import '../index.js'`
  of the ES module wrapper, which then reads `undefined` from `globalThis` and throws on import.

Also replaces `export =` in `index.d.ts` with `export default`: our declaration build can't bundle
CommonJS declaration syntax.

